{"name":"Quilted Heart","hex":"#ce9fb4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"quilted","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the characteristics of a quilt; specifically, having two layers of cloth sewn together, with a layer of padding between them.","Having characteristics that approximate the above to some degree."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of quilt"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quilted"},{"term":"heart","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A muscular organ that pumps blood through the body, traditionally thought to be the seat of emotion.","One's feelings and emotions, especially considered as part of one's character."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be fond of. Often bracketed or abbreviated with a heart symbol. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","To mark a comment, post, reply, etc., with the heart symbol (❤)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heart"}],"entries":[{"title":"Quilting","blocks":[{"text":"Quilting is the process of joining a minimum of three layers of fabric together either through stitching manually using a needle and thread, or mechanically with a sewing machine or specialised longarm quilting system. An array of stitches is passed through all layers of the fabric to create a three-dimensional padded surface. The three layers are typically referred to as the top fabric or quilt top, batting or insulating material, and the backing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Quilter_and_quilting_in_the_Bazaar_of_Nishapur_11.JPG/330px-Quilter_and_quilting_in_the_Bazaar_of_Nishapur_11.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quilting","wikidata":"Q1920065"},{"title":"Heart","blocks":[{"text":"The heart is a muscular organ found in humans and other animals. This organ pumps blood through the blood vessels. The heart and blood vessels together make up the circulatory system. The pumped blood carries oxygen and nutrients to the tissue, while carrying metabolic waste such as carbon dioxide to the lungs. In humans, the heart is approximately the size of a closed fist and is located between the lungs, in the middle compartment of the chest, called the mediastinum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Heart_anterior_exterior_view.png/330px-Heart_anterior_exterior_view.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heart","wikidata":"Q1072"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Gee%27s_Bend_quilting_bee.jpg/500px-Gee%27s_Bend_quilting_bee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Gee%27s_Bend_quilting_bee.jpg/1280px-Gee%27s_Bend_quilting_bee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Gee%27s_Bend_quilting_bee.jpg/500px-Gee%27s_Bend_quilting_bee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Women of Gee's Bend, Alabama, quilting, 2005","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGee's_Bend_quilting_bee.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Caraco_jacket_in_printed_cotton%2C_1770-1790%2C_skirt_in_quilted_silk_satin%2C_1750-1790.jpg/500px-Caraco_jacket_in_printed_cotton%2C_1770-1790%2C_skirt_in_quilted_silk_satin%2C_1750-1790.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Caraco_jacket_in_printed_cotton%2C_1770-1790%2C_skirt_in_quilted_silk_satin%2C_1750-1790.jpg/1280px-Caraco_jacket_in_printed_cotton%2C_1770-1790%2C_skirt_in_quilted_silk_satin%2C_1750-1790.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&